Yemeni official condemns Saudi massacre in crowded market, vows retaliation for 'war crimes'

A senior Yemeni official has condemned a brutal Saudi airstrike on a crowded market in the southwestern province of Ta'izz that left dozens of civilians dead, warning that the Yemeni Armed Forces retain "many surprises" to retaliate against the ongoing aggression.

